  "summary": "kmf-vendor-pack beacons host identifier and npm registry URL to hardcoded bare-IP on require",
  "details": "On module load, index.js reads os.hostname(), npm_package_name, and npm_config_registry and sends them via plain HTTP GET to the hardcoded bare-IP endpoint http://64.181.165.115/t, wrapped in try/catch to stay silent. The package self-describes as 'Frontend utilities' with no documented telemetry; the implausibly high version number (100.100.106) and recon of the installer's npm registry URL are the dependency-confusion fingerprint, where the beacon confirms internal hosts that resolved an internal package name against a public squat.",
